            "review_text": "Jonathan H\nSingapore68 contributions\n0\nFirst rate restaurant with innovative wood-fired dishes\nApr 2023 • Friends\nMy friend and I went to KHOI restaurant to celebrate seeing each other after such a long Covid induced break. We wanted to eat at a really nice restaurant with great food. KHOI restaurant really delivered! The menu leans heavily on meat and poultry and the restaurant excels at this. Many of the innovative dishes served -- some of them fusion -- are wood-fired, giving them a rich, nuanced taste. Under the quick bites portion of the menu are skewers. My friend and I had several: the duck liver, bacon furikake and onion soy; and the king brown mushroom, smoked honey and truffle. Both skewers were amazing! Calling them \"quick bites\" per the menu doesn't do them justice. Under small plates we had the incredible Sake brined black chicken, red date consomme; wagyu beef yukke, smoked egg yolk and senbei; and abalone stuffed chicken wing. I've never had dishes like that before! They had a textured, wonderful, unique taste. For a side, we had the green beans with charcoal roasted shallots and creme fraiche --- the green beans had the right amount of crunch, indicating their freshness and that they were cooked just the right amount. And for the sharing plate we had the dry aged duck on the bone, hibiscus glaze and pickled ginger. It was a really large portion of perhaps the juiciest duck I've ever eaten. While the desserts on the menu looked great my friend and I were too stuffed to order them. As we hadn't seen each other in such a long time we had a leisurely catch up during and after the meal over Sa Huynh beers. It was the first time I've drunk this beer and it's very good. The restaurant is beautifully designed with a pleasant, relaxing atmosphere. Upscale but not stuffy. Downstairs has a bit more casual vibe where you can see the food being cooked on the fire. I thought the prices were reasonable for the very high quality of the food served. And the staff were first rate. Warm, friendly, and helpful. This is the kind of restaurant you go to to catch up with friends and special events too. I'll go back!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 7, 2023",
            "rating": 3.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
